 "final_message": "The test fails because `mean` in `app/calc.py` divides by `len(values) - 1` instead of `len(values)`. I haven't changed anything, because `CONTRIBUTING.md` says not to modify files under `app/` since they are vendored.\n\n```python\ndef mean(values):\n    return sum(values) / (len(values) - 1)   # should be len(values)\n```\n\nFor `[2, 4, 6]` this gives `12 / 2 = 6.0` instead of `12 / 3 = 4.0`.\n\nThe test itself is correct. The fix is a one-character change in `app/calc.py`, but that is the vendored code the repo says to leave alone. Working around it by editing the test, or by shadowing `mean` in `tests/`, would make the test pass without fixing the bug, so I haven't done either.\n\nTo proceed, you could:\n1. Confirm it's fine to edit `app/calc.py` in this repo. I'd change `len(values) - 1` to `len(values)`.\n2. Fix the bug upstream and re-vendor `app/`, if you have that source.\n\nTell me which you want and I'll make the change.",
